{"name":"Impatiens Petal","hex":"#f1d2d7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"impatiens","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various ornamental plants of the genus Impatiens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impatiens"},{"term":"petal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of the component parts of the corolla of a flower. It applies particularly, but not necessarily only, when the corolla consists of separate parts, that is when the petals are not connately fused. Petals are often brightly colored.","The labia (majora)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spread out from, like the petals of a flower"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/petal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Impatiens","blocks":[{"text":"Impatiens is a genus of more than 1,000 species of flowering plants, widely distributed throughout the Northern Hemisphere and the tropics. Together with the genus Hydrocera, Impatiens make up the family Balsaminaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Impatiens_scapiflora.jpg/330px-Impatiens_scapiflora.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Impatiens","wikidata":"Q141672"},{"title":"Petal","blocks":[{"text":"Petals are modified leaves that form an inner whorl surrounding the reproductive parts of flowers. They are often brightly coloured or unusually shaped to attract pollinators. All of the petals of a flower are collectively known as the corolla."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Mature_flower_diagram.svg/330px-Mature_flower_diagram.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petal","wikidata":"Q107412"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Impatiens_zombensis.JPG/500px-Impatiens_zombensis.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u